{"data": [{"article": {"title": "2026 AI Infrastructure and Silicon: The Year in Review"}, "author_id": "1600530338920415232", "created_at": "2026-11-09T01:07:36.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119597742867480910"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/i/article/2119…", "end": 230, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/i/article/2119595549523431425", "start": 207, "status": 404, "unwound_url": "https://x.com/i/article/2119595549523431425", "url": "https://t.co/Z4oCzktY4b"}]}, "id": "2119597742867480910", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 1082, "like_count": 6, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 8, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "2026 AI Infrastructure and Silicon: The Year in Review\n\nFull institutional synthesis covering the Macro Ledger Shift, the Physical Laws of Inference, the 96 EB Server DRAM Deficit, and the Qualcomm Defense. https://t.co/Z4oCzktY4b", "url": "https://x.com/LiDaosen/status/2119597742867480910"}, {"author_id": "1600530338920415232", "created_at": "2026-11-09T15:44:26.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119818403879792762"], "entities": {"cashtags": [{"end": 33, "start": 30, "tag": "BE"}, {"end": 40, "start": 35, "tag": "ALAB"}, {"end": 47, "start": 42, "tag": "VICR"}, {"end": 58, "start": 53, "tag": "COHR"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/CKCapitalxx/st…", "end": 299, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/CKCapitalxx/status/2119815347662417922", "start": 276, "url": "https://t.co/DxMoI07b4a"}]}, "id": "2119818403879792762", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 952, "like_count": 4, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119815347662417922", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "The simultaneous rally across $BE, $ALAB, $VICR, and $COHR illustrates a core buy-side rule: when physical laws govern computing, hardware bottlenecks capture the economic rent.\n\nWhile retail debates GPU market share (Nvidia vs AMD vs custom ASICs), this basket monetizes the https://t.co/DxMoI07b4a", "url": "https://x.com/LiDaosen/status/2119818403879792762"}, {"author_id": "951956184", "created_at": "2026-11-10T03:54:35.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120002152647233924", "2120006437871210700"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/j8a1qvo5be", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/ramthamedia/status/2120002152647233924/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120002142836822016", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/j8a1qvo5be"}]}, "id": "2120002152647233924", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 103, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "🚨 THE AI HARDWARE COLD WAR: Why China risked a nation-state espionage operation for Nvidia Blackwell silicon, and why the $177 dip is the most misunderstood valuation dislocation in modern market history.\n\nA forensic breakdown of the Megaspeed probe, TSMC packaging chokepoints, https://t.co/j8a1qvo5be", "url": "https://x.com/ramthamedia/status/2120002152647233924"}, {"author_id": "951956184", "created_at": "2026-11-10T04:11:37.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120002152647233924", "2120006437871210700"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/gc0HzXXdrf", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/ramthamedia/status/2120006437871210700/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120006428106899456", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/gc0HzXXdrf"}]}, "id": "2120006437871210700", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 803, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "🚨 THE AI HARDWARE COLD WAR: Why China risked a nation-state espionage operation for Nvidia Blackwell silicon, and why the $177 dip is the most misunderstood valuation dislocation in modern market history.\n\nA forensic breakdown of the Megaspeed probe, TSMC packaging chokepoints, https://t.co/gc0HzXXdrf", "url": "https://x.com/ramthamedia/status/2120006437871210700"}, {"author_id": "54037704", "created_at": "2026-11-09T23:01:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119928485024293224"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/fr58xVvUoV", "end": 221, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/vexxhost/status/2119928485024293224/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2119928375536209920", "start": 198, "url": "https://t.co/fr58xVvUoV"}]}, "id": "2119928485024293224", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 15, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Signals worth a dashboard panel on an AI cluster, layer by layer from GPU to training jobs. Checkpoint age is an easy one to miss, and it tells you how much work a single worker failure would cost. https://t.co/fr58xVvUoV", "url": "https://x.com/vexxhost/status/2119928485024293224"}, {"author_id": "1328890851590692864", "created_at": "2026-11-09T07:13:37.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119689853378167001"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 49, "start": 37, "tag": "NVIDIAAIDAY"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/txdLSi1H50", "end": 299, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/NAVER__Cloud/status/2119689853378167001/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2119689563870507010", "start": 276, "url": "https://t.co/txdLSi1H50"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/txdLSi1H50", "end": 299, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/NAVER__Cloud/status/2119689853378167001/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2119689617834483712", "start": 276, "url": "https://t.co/txdLSi1H50"}]}, "id": "2119689853378167001", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 102, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Thousands of GPUs, 365 days a year 📍 #NVIDIAAIDAY  Seoul 2026\n\nByungjun Kim, Head of the Cloud Infrastructure Center at NAVER Cloud, took the stage today to share lessons from running GPU infrastructure at scale.\n\nHe shared how we brought a 2,096-GPU NVIDIA B300 cluster from https://t.co/txdLSi1H50", "url": "https://x.com/NAVER__Cloud/status/2119689853378167001"}, {"author_id": "1896482241280368640", "created_at": "2026-11-10T15:51:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120182453587595416"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 186, "start": 181, "tag": "H200"}, {"end": 193, "start": 187, "tag": "AIGPU"}, {"end": 202, "start": 194, "tag": "Compute"}, {"end": 207, "start": 203, "tag": "LLM"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/nrV7vo2p6c", "end": 231, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/moonpixie565/status/2120182453587595416/video/1", "media_key": "7_2120182371664478208", "start": 208, "url": "https://t.co/nrV7vo2p6c"}]}, "id": "2120182453587595416", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Bored with H100? Swap for 8× H200🔥\nBoost your AI training &amp; inference with H200’s high memory throughput.\nReady-built GPU server on hand for your AI cluster. Message for quote.\n#H200 #AIGPU #Compute #LLM https://t.co/nrV7vo2p6c", "url": "https://x.com/moonpixie565/status/2120182453587595416"}, {"author_id": "127042462", "created_at": "2026-11-10T14:53:33.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120167987550498964"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/elonmusk/statu…", "end": 298, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/elonmusk/status/2120102767624880364", "start": 275, "url": "https://t.co/V2YjIXDkXB"}]}, "id": "2120167987550498964", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120102767624880364", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Starlink software turning out to be good for training superintelligence is a wild crossover. Moving massive data across thousands of satellites and moving it across a giant GPU cluster might be closer problems than people think. Real edge for Grok or just a fun coincidence? https://t.co/V2YjIXDkXB", "url": "https://x.com/Notorious_corbz/status/2120167987550498964"}, {"author_id": "47048426", "created_at": "2026-11-09T19:20:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119872666673021135"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/Fku9I2fYA2", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/hinadixit/status/2119872666673021135/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2119872663267274752", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/Fku9I2fYA2"}]}, "id": "2119872666673021135", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 85, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "At CoRL, the robotics number I care about is the cost of learning a usable motion—not the size of the training cluster. Berkeley’s SuperMimic reports beating SONIC’s released motion-tracking checkpoint after 3 hours on one H100; SONIC trained for 7 days on 128 L40 GPUs. That’s 3 https://t.co/Fku9I2fYA2", "url": "https://x.com/hinadixit/status/2119872666673021135"}, {"author_id": "2071862364966678528", "created_at": "2026-11-10T16:32:07.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120192793587097782"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/PCuu2ajFuk", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Chillha123/status/2120192793587097782/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120192775224483840", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/PCuu2ajFuk"}]}, "id": "2120192793587097782", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 13, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "💻 BITTORRENT - ANCHORING STORAGE AND DATA TRANSPORT FOR DECENTRALIZED AI COMPUTE\n\nThe rapid expansion of artificial intelligence requires not only specialized GPU compute hardware but also robust infrastructure for storing, distributing, and retrieving massive training datasets. https://t.co/PCuu2ajFuk", "url": "https://x.com/Chillha123/status/2120192793587097782"}, {"author_id": "442390892", "created_at": "2026-11-09T15:29:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119814712515018954"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/Ct01ld9MdZ", "end": 299, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Richdegen67/status/2119814712515018954/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2119814704260628480", "start": 276, "url": "https://t.co/Ct01ld9MdZ"}]}, "id": "2119814712515018954", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 31109, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "🌐 SECURING DECENTRALIZED COMPUTE CLUSTERS ON TRON WITH WINKLINK DePIN TELEMETRY\n\nDecentralized GPU compute networks enable artificial intelligence developers to rent compute clusters for training neural network models using cryptocurrency payments. DePIN networks deployed on https://t.co/Ct01ld9MdZ", "url": "https://x.com/Richdegen67/status/2119814712515018954"}, {"author_id": "1553496396464005127", "created_at": "2026-11-09T21:47:59.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119909895134712235"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/CoreWeave/stat…", "end": 301, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/CoreWeave/status/2119897909336445151", "start": 278, "url": "https://t.co/JSTSfFdzUr"}]}, "id": "2119909895134712235", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 123, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119897909336445151", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "CoreWeave just launched their official skills. Congrats, genuinely. Here's my side of the road to today.\n\nIn October, CoreWeave's counsel wrote to me about my community skill \"CoreWeave CI Integration.\" They asked me to rename it to \"Unofficial CI Integration for CoreWeave\" so https://t.co/JSTSfFdzUr", "url": "https://x.com/jeremylongshore/status/2119909895134712235"}, {"author_id": "208238459", "created_at": "2026-11-10T13:55:23.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120153350280790313"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/elonmusk/statu…", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/elonmusk/status/2120102767624880364", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/Y3jFGasyZw"}]}, "id": "2120153350280790313", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 8, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120102767624880364", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "A satellite network and a GPU cluster share the same enemy: the one slow link.\n\nStarlink moves traffic across roughly 11,000 satellites whose neighbors never stop moving, so routes keep changing and failures get routed around with no human in the loop.\n\nTraining a frontier model https://t.co/Y3jFGasyZw", "url": "https://x.com/Quangjin21/status/2120153350280790313"}, {"author_id": "266259493", "created_at": "2026-11-09T20:11:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119885487003607272"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/sundarpichai/s…", "end": 301, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/sundarpichai/status/2119857335871164769", "start": 278, "url": "https://t.co/leqfUf2wW5"}]}, "id": "2119885487003607272", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 228, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119857335871164769", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Four distinct TPU systems in a single generation, inside twelve months. That's the number Sundar Pichai led with today, and it's a strange thing to brag about until you remember what \"one generation, one year\" used to mean in chips: a multi-year tape-out cycle, not a quarterly https://t.co/leqfUf2wW5", "url": "https://x.com/stretchcloud/status/2119885487003607272"}, {"author_id": "59834142", "created_at": "2026-11-10T14:34:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120163150116933860"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/swann_bessa/st…", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/swann_bessa/status/2119923855204774121", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/PV6Ip6SBjE"}]}, "id": "2120163150116933860", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 181, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 1}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119923855204774121", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Classic k-means is still the slow step when you train a vector index or cluster a pile of embeddings. e-means, from Meta FAIR and now inside faiss, is a drop-in replacement for Lloyd's algorithm. It does many small mini-batch updates with moving averages, and the batch and step https://t.co/PV6Ip6SBjE", "url": "https://x.com/carlosearias/status/2120163150116933860"}, {"author_id": "2092934142896078848", "created_at": "2026-11-09T14:21:52.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119797625780379793"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/T0EDJp0kQt", "end": 301, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/shaoxiao_si/status/2119797625780379793/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2119797420792135680", "start": 278, "url": "https://t.co/T0EDJp0kQt"}, {"display_url": "x.com/Google/status/…", "end": 325, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/Google/status/2119788086490001906", "start": 302, "url": "https://t.co/se9y5xjYPt"}]}, "id": "2119797625780379793", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 10, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119788086490001906", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Google posted two new 8th-gen TPU systems: TPU 8i Max and TPU 8tx.\n\nAmin Vahdat's Nov 9 blog: first time four 8th-gen TPU systems in one year, joining April's TPU 8t (scale-up training) and TPU 8i (low-latency reasoning). 8i Max puts two 8i chips in one package: 2x compute, 2x https://t.co/T0EDJp0kQt https://t.co/se9y5xjYPt", "url": "https://x.com/shaoxiao_si/status/2119797625780379793"}, {"author_id": "996725486427561991", "created_at": "2026-11-10T10:28:43.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120101339112067342"], "entities": {"cashtags": [{"end": 5, "start": 0, "tag": "WYFI"}, {"end": 98, "start": 93, "tag": "NVDA"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/qrXdhoaOik", "end": 299, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Jessica869f/status/2120101339112067342/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120101323190460416", "start": 276, "url": "https://t.co/qrXdhoaOik"}]}, "id": "2120101339112067342", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 979, "like_count": 9, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "$WYFI Whitefiber working on retrofitting stranded telco and metro assets and guess what .... $NVDA is looking to finance a bunch of deals doing this exact thing. Watch for news between these two companies might be coming. \n \nMany telecom and metro facilities sit on power and https://t.co/qrXdhoaOik", "url": "https://x.com/Jessica869f/status/2120101339112067342"}, {"author_id": "147445380", "created_at": "2026-11-10T05:11:26.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120021492327149855"], "id": "2120021492327149855", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 26, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Building India's own GPU in two years is the hardware half of the job. I'd bet the software stack takes longer.\n\nMeitY Secretary S. Krishnan said in an interview reported by IANS on Monday that India is targeting a homegrown GPU in roughly 24 months, under India Semiconductor", "url": "https://x.com/me_deepu/status/2120021492327149855"}, {"author_id": "2093444093531865088", "created_at": "2026-11-09T20:45:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119894096571756677"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "B.AI is the foundational economic infrastructure for AI Agents. Access global top-tier AI models anonymously via our borderless payment system. We provide a unified API and settlement network, empowering artificial intelligence with true financial autonomy.", "display_url": "B.AI", "end": 91, "expanded_url": "https://B.AI", "images": [{"height": 1200, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120215188917940224/oCkmmYIz?format=png&name=orig", "width": 2400}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/212021518891794